From 44a2e4f74f30290ee5874c143e70d183ef3ab2a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:00:36 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [guilib] Settle subpixel textures a moment after they
 stop

Deciding "moving" from one render to the next snaps the texture
whenever a render sees the rect it saw last time: a repeated frame
time, an easing step too small to change the rect, or a second render
of the same frame (stereo 3D draws each eye, dirty-region solvers 1 and
2 draw each region), which then mismatches the first. Decide it once
per frame in Process() instead, keep the fractional position for 200 ms
after the last change, and dirty the texture once when it snaps.

Assisted-By: Claude
---
 xbmc/guilib/GUIImage.dox   |  2 +-
 xbmc/guilib/GUITexture.cpp | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 xbmc/guilib/GUITexture.h   |  6 ++++--
 3 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/guilib/GUIImage.dox b/xbmc/guilib/GUIImage.dox
index 8c73684573..1c80fa8326 100644
--- a/xbmc/guilib/GUIImage.dox
+++ b/xbmc/guilib/GUIImage.dox
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ For the tags "texture" and "bordertexture", the following attributes are availab
 | background    | Used on the <b>`<imagepath>`</b> tag. When set to "true", this forces the image to be loaded via the large texture manager (except for textures located in Textures.xbt).
 | diffuse       | Specifies a diffuse texture which is "modulated" or multiplied with the texture in order to give specific effects, such as making the image gain transparency, or tint it in various ways. As it's applied per-pixel many effects are possible, the most popular being by a transparent reflection which slowly gets more and more opaque. This is achieved using a WHITE image where the transparency increases as you move down the texture.
 | colordiffuse  | This specifies the color to be used for the texture basis. It's is specified in hexadecimal notation using the AARRGGBB format. If you define <b>`<texture colordiffuse="FFFFAAFF">texture.png</texture>`</b> (magenta), the image will be given a magenta tint when rendered. You can also specify this as a name from the colour theme, or you can also use $VAR and $INFO for dynamic values.
-| subpixel      | When set to "true", the texture keeps its fractional screen position while it moves instead of being snapped to whole pixels, so slow zoom and slide animations move smoothly rather than in one pixel steps. Once it stops moving it is snapped again. Best suited to photos and artwork that move; edges and 1 pixel lines are softer during motion, and labels drawn over the texture still snap to whole pixels. Defaults to "false".
+| subpixel      | When set to "true", the texture keeps its fractional screen position while it moves instead of being snapped to whole pixels, so slow zoom and slide animations move smoothly rather than in one pixel steps. Shortly after it stops moving it is snapped again. Best suited to photos and artwork that move; edges and 1 pixel lines are softer during motion, and labels drawn over the texture still snap to whole pixels. Defaults to "false".
 
